Description: Querencia Desktop – classic GNOME 2 style desktop (metapackage, alpha)
 Querencia Desktop is a classic desktop in the style of GNOME 2 /
 Ubuntu 10.04, written in Rust with GTK 4 for Wayland on the labwc
 compositor.
 .
 This metapackage installs all components: session, panel and desktop,
 session dialog with screen lock and polkit agent, notifications,
 settings, file manager, terminal, screenshot tool, text editor, image
 viewer, calculator, system monitor, file search and the software manager;
 the PDF viewer (querencia-dokumente) is recommended. Afterwards
 "Querencia Desktop" can be chosen in the session list of the display
 manager (GDM shows it after a restart). No display manager is installed
 or reconfigured.
 .
 The mouse pointer theme (DMZ) and the DejaVu fonts come from the
 distribution packages dmz-cursor-theme and fonts-dejavu (recommended:
 fonts-dejavu-extra); this package ships neither fonts nor pointers.
 .
 Recommended: PipeWire for sound (volume applet), NetworkManager for the
 network applet (with systemd-networkd it only shows the state) and
 notify-send (libnotify-bin). On a server installation the recommended
 packages pull in about 360 further packages from the archive, among them
 Avahi, wsdd and the X helpers for Xwayland; apt --no-install-recommends
 installs the desktop without them.
 .
 Querencia Desktop is developed with AI tools; every change is reviewed
 and accepted by the project owner.
 This is an alpha release, not intended for production use.
